  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Farming with Adapted Crops and Soils</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Farming with Adapted Crops and Soils supports greater climate resilience for smallholder farmers in the Pacific. It covers:

1. The Pacific vision for Adapted Crops and Soils (PACS), which seeks to build a resilient food system grounded in diverse, nutritious and climate-adapted crops grown in healthy soils and landscapes.

2. Climate Resilient Farming in the Pacific, which supports Pacific Farmer Organisations to strengthen resilience, food and water security of Pacific farmers by helping them adapt to the threat of changing climate and natural disasters.

3. Access to climate resilient planting material and other farm inputs.

4. Agricultural research and climate modelling to inform investment in more resilient food systems.</narrative>
  </description>
